{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1447458-porting-v5-mechanics-to-v20-and-vice-versa","id":1447458,"title":"Porting V5 mechanics to V20, and vice versa.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-05-04T15:08:55-07:00","id":1447458,"title":"Porting V5 mechanics to V20, and vice versa.","content":"Title says it all. I recently started reading V20, and other 20th edition books, and was wondering if anyone has tried porting the better parts of either V5 or V20 to each other?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/7.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26764-vilenecromancer","name":"Vilenecromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26764_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"247"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-04T18:01:34-07:00","id":1447501,"title":"","content":"I\u2019ve got some options based off replacing the clan weaknesses with the V5 banes (mostly... I swapped the V5 Ravnos bane for one were they lose willpower if they don\u2019t engage with their compulsion; not necessarily a criminal vice; the Ravnos in our game is a shopaholic). and some adapting of generation so it isn\u2019t a background but generations 8-16 are instead balanced by size of blood pool, bane potency and certain merits gained by the thin bloods.<br /> <br /> I\u2019ve also tweaked a few discipline ranks with powers I think were better implementations (ex. Presence 1 as basically Potence for interaction checks with Wits+Awareness to recognize you\u2019re being influenced and can cancel the effects with a point of Willpower).<br /> <br /> Most of my adaptations though are plot points like the destruction of Vienna or the Fall of London, only instead of happening 10-15 years ago, they\u2019re either just happening or in the near future.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-05T01:25:15-07:00","id":1447541,"title":"","content":"Hunger Dice can easily be added to V20 (+1 for when you spend each of the last five blood points of your blood pool). You can fudge the numbers a bit more if you want a closer correlation (e.g., have Hunger 1 at 9 blood points, for example, then Hunger 2 at 7, Hunger 3 at 5, Hunger 4 at 3 and Hunger 5 at 1, with auto-Frenzy at zero blood points).<br /> <br /> You can easily make alternate Discipline powers be Devotions you purchase for a fixed price or take instead of the main power (but do allow more than one power per dot).<br /> <br /> You can make stronger Banes for lower Generations without using Blood Potency. There are already rules in V20 for gaining Methuselah's Thirst (were they in Elysium and then reprinted in one of the DA books?).<br /> <br /> You could apply a Compulsion whenever a player botches a roll that uses blood (e.g., Discipline activations or any roll with blood buffed Attributes). Or use Bestial Failures and Messy Criticals in these situations instead.<br /> <br /> You can add Touchstones (human and non-human) as a bulwark against Humanity or Path loss. Gain an extra dice or two when you acted to protect a Touchstone. <br /> <br /> You can add Chronicle Tenets as additional Path 'ethics' for the whole table, on the assumption that letting your mates get away with bad stuff also soils your own soul.<br /> <br /> You can make the difference between your current Path level and the sin you violate a modifier to your Degeneration roll (this exists in some versions of the rules anyway), giving you much the same benefit as the Stains system. V5's Stains modifiers could be used as well or instead, though, with a little tweaking.<br /> <br /> You can crib V5's combat, or better yet, use V20DA's streamlined combat rules with a few things pinched from V5 as needed.<br /> <br /> And, of course, you can easily use the V5 dice pool system (all dice need to be 6+ to succeed, perhaps with 10s as doubles and 1s subtracting to keep the maths averaging out at half a success per dice).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-05T08:41:53-07:00","id":1447579,"title":"","content":"Hunger dice/Clan compulsions/Messy criticals make for a decent derangement/flaw . To simulate these, You set increments on the blood chart and can give players &quot;Red Dice&quot; accordingly. <br /> <br /> You can 'buy' convictions like virtue dots, and add them to conscience/self control/courage rolls when appropriate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-05T13:53:44-07:00","id":1447623,"title":"","content":"If you're willing to search this forum, there's been a number of port attempts.<br /> <br /> Personally, I would plug VtR 2e as a book to get if you're considering the process because mechanically it can feel closer to V20, but has similar design ideas to V5, and can be a great source of options for ways to work things from one to the other depending on what you're trying to port.<br /> <br /> For example, if you want to have Bane Severity be a thing in V20, don't want to bring in Blood Potency, and don't want it to be tied to Generation? VtR 2e actually had the idea without giving it a name. In VtR 2e all banes (even sunlight) are tied to your Humanity rating. The lower it goes, the worse things get (in fact the Clan banes in VtR 2e don't even activate until you drop to Humanity 6 for the first time). Probably the most simple is the Gangrel Bane: the Feral Curse. Their maximum dice-pool to resist frenzy is capped by Humanity (which is, yes, very different from the VtM idea of the Gangrel, but it's easy to see how it works).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-05T23:20:54-07:00","id":1447696,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1447458-porting-v5-mechanics-to-v20-and-vice-versa?p=1447623#post1447623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you're willing to search this forum, there's been a number of port attempts.<br /> <br /> Personally, I would plug VtR 2e as a book to get if you're considering the process because mechanically it can feel closer to V20, but has similar design ideas to V5, and can be a great source of options for ways to work things from one to the other depending on what you're trying to port.<br /> <br /> For example, if you want to have Bane Severity be a thing in V20, don't want to bring in Blood Potency, and don't want it to be tied to Generation? VtR 2e actually had the idea without giving it a name. In VtR 2e all banes (even sunlight) are tied to your Humanity rating. The lower it goes, the worse things get (in fact the Clan banes in VtR 2e don't even activate until you drop to Humanity 6 for the first time). Probably the most simple is the Gangrel Bane: the Feral Curse. Their maximum dice-pool to resist frenzy is capped by Humanity (which is, yes, very different from the VtM idea of the Gangrel, but it's easy to see how it works).</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, yes, I would second this. VTR2e is the superior d10-based system for vampires. Its setting is intentionally skimpy but there's enough stuff out there to easily port over VTM's setting (search the forums for 'Masquiem' and '13 Licks').","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-06T17:38:03-07:00","id":1447737,"title":"","content":"I have backported some of V5's Compulsions into my V20 chronicle, as I like the idea of each Clan's blood carrying along with its curse the psychic imprint (resonance?) of that clan's Founder. So far I have only written up rules for the Clans most prominent in my chronicle and will probably never get around to doing them all, and I altered the Nosferatu compulsion into something much darker which I feel better suits the personality of Absimiliard.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26710-ventrue-busboy","name":"Ventrue Busboy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26710_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-07T00:35:36-07:00","id":1447779,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ventrue Busboy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1447458-porting-v5-mechanics-to-v20-and-vice-versa?p=1447737#post1447737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have backported some of V5's Compulsions into my V20 chronicle, as I like the idea of each Clan's blood carrying along with its curse the psychic imprint (resonance?) of that clan's Founder. So far I have only written up rules for the Clans most prominent in my chronicle and will probably never get around to doing them all, and I altered the Nosferatu compulsion into something much darker which I feel better suits the personality of Absimiliard.</div> </div> </div> </div>Would you care to share?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}